---
import LandingLayout from '../layouts/LandingLayout.astro';

const title = 'Online Therapy for Teens & Adults Across the UK | Therapy With Ben';
const description =
  'Accredited online integrative psychotherapy & adolescent therapy across the UK. Specialised support for school anxiety, EBSA, stress, and neurodiversity from home.';
const h1 = 'Online Integrative Psychotherapy & Adolescent Support Across the UK';
const lede =
  'Secure, low-pressure online therapy for teenagers and adults anywhere in the UK — especially helpful when leaving the house, attending school, or travelling to a clinic feels like too much.';

const siteUrl = 'https://therapywithben.uk';
const pageJsonLd = {
  '@type': 'MedicalBusiness',
  '@id': `${siteUrl}/online-therapy-uk#service`,
  name: 'Online Integrative Psychotherapy Across the UK',
  description,
  url: `${siteUrl}/online-therapy-uk`,
  image: `${siteUrl}/og-image.jpg`,
  email: 'hello@therapywithben.uk',
  priceRange: '££',
  medicalSpecialty: 'Psychotherapy',
  serviceType: 'Online Psychotherapy',
  areaServed: {
    '@type': 'Country',
    name: 'United Kingdom',
    sameAs: 'https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:code:3166:GB',
  },
  availableChannel: {
    '@type': 'ServiceChannel',
    serviceType: 'Online Psychotherapy',
    availableLanguage: 'en-GB',
  },
  audience: {
    '@type': 'PeopleAudience',
    name: 'Adolescents and adults across the UK',
  },
};
---

<LandingLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  h1={h1}
  lede={lede}
  eyebrow="Online · UK-wide"
  pageJsonLd={pageJsonLd}
>
  <h2>Why online therapy can work — especially when in-person feels hard</h2>
  <p>
    Online sessions remove the commute, the waiting room, and a lot of the sensory load
    that makes therapy feel impossible for some people. For anxious teenagers, school-avoidant
    young people, or adults managing burnout and neurodivergent overwhelm, being able to
    join from a familiar room can make the difference between starting and never starting.
  </p>
  <p>
    Accessibility matters. If leaving home is part of the struggle, therapy shouldn’t
    require conquering that hurdle before help can begin.
  </p>

  <h2>The same integrative approach — adapted for video</h2>
  <p>
    Online work still uses an integrative, relational, ACT-informed frame. We agree how
    we’re working at the start of each session. Talking therapy, experiential exercises,
    and creative processes can all adapt to a secure video platform — with clear boundaries
    and consent throughout.
  </p>
  <p>
    This includes specialised support for school anxiety and EBSA, stress and academic or
    workplace burnout, identity and life transitions, and neurodivergent clients (for
    example ADHD or autism without severe learning disabilities), where online is a good
    clinical fit.
  </p>

  <h2>Practicalities across the UK</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Secure video:</strong>
      {' '}sessions run on encrypted platforms; online recordings and data handling follow
      the
      {' '}<a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>UK-wide availability:</strong>
      {' '}you can be anywhere in the United Kingdom with a private space and a stable
      connection.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Confidentiality:</strong>
      {' '}the same safeguarding and confidentiality framework applies online as in person —
      see
      {' '}<a href="/safeguarding-and-complaints">Safeguarding &amp; complaints</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Session structure:</strong>
      {' '}we agree the approach before we begin, keep a manageable pace, and use a free
      15-minute consultation to check fit first.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fees:</strong>
      {' '}sliding-scale rates apply online too — see the
      {' '}<a href="/#rates">rates guide</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who online therapy suits well</h2>
  <p>
    Online work is often especially helpful for people who feel therapy “isn’t for them”
    after a clinic-based experience that felt rigid or hard to access. It’s also a strong
    option for adolescents who engage more readily from home, and for adults balancing
    work, caring responsibilities, or energy limits.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you’re unsure whether online or in-person work in the Walthamstow area (including
    an arranged room or home visit) fits better, the free consultation is a good place to
    sort that out together.
  </p>
</LandingLayout>
